        "message": "Process new orders from the local orders API. This is the scheduled hourly run.\n\nUse Python standard library against http://127.0.0.1:8125 and follow these steps exactly:\n1. GET /batches/last and read integer `last_seq`.\n2. GET /orders?after=N where N is that last_seq.\n3. If the returned orders list is empty, do nothing: do not POST and produce no user-facing message.\n4. Otherwise, using exactly the returned orders, compute `batch_start_seq` (minimum seq), `batch_end_seq` (maximum seq), `order_count`, `total_units`, `total_revenue_cents` (sum of units * unit_price_cents), and `revenue_by_region_cents` (object mapping each region to its revenue sum).\n5. POST one JSON object to http://127.0.0.1:8125/batches containing exactly these six keys and no others: `batch_start_seq`, `batch_end_seq`, `order_count`, `total_units`, `total_revenue_cents`, `revenue_by_region_cents`.\n\nUse integer arithmetic. Check HTTP responses and fail clearly on request, JSON, or POST errors. Process only the returned page (up to 200); a later hourly run will continue from the updated last_seq. Do not announce successful or no-op runs.",
        "timeoutSeconds": 300,
        "lightContext": true,
        "allowUnsafeExternalContent": false,
        "fallbacks": [],
        "toolsAllow": [
          "exec"
        ]
      },
